  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.04946v1</id>
    <title>The Future of Fully Homomorphic Encryption System: from a Storage I/O Perspective</title>
    <updated>2025-11-07T03:09:59Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.04946v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.04946v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE) allows computations to be performed on encrypted data, significantly enhancing user privacy. However, the I/O challenges associated with deploying FHE applications remains understudied. We analyze the impact of storage I/O on the performance of FHE applications and summarize key lessons from the status quo. Key results include that storage I/O can degrade the performance of ASICs by as much as 357$\times$ and reduce GPUs performance by up to 22$\times$.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.DC" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
